### PaySQL REST API examples
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension, or copy into curl.
### Set @host and @token for your environment.

@host = http://localhost:8080/ords/paysql/v1
@token = REPLACE_WITH_BEARER_TOKEN

### List employees
GET {{host}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get one employee
GET {{host}}/employees/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create an employee
POST {{host}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "EMP0011",
  "first_name": "New",
  "last_name": "Hire",
  "email": "new.hire@example.com",
  "dept_code": "ENG",
  "grade_code": "J2",
  "hire_date": "2026-02-01"
}

### An employee's payslip history
GET {{host}}/employees/1/payslips
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Payslip detail (line items)
GET {{host}}/payslips/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### --- Pay-run lifecycle ---

### 1. Calculate a pay run for a period
POST {{host}}/payruns
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "period_code": "2026-01" }

### 2. Approve (use the pay_run_id returned above)
POST {{host}}/payruns/1/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "approved_by": "alice" }

### 3. Post
POST {{host}}/payruns/1/post
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Pay from a fund
POST {{host}}/payruns/1/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fund_code": "MAIN" }

### 5. Close
POST {{host}}/payruns/1/close
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Payroll register for a run
GET {{host}}/payruns/1/register
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
